id: pm-5iwfkj
title: "GH-1354: Linked-test snapshot mode drops nested package dependencies and breaks monorepo acceptance"
description: Published linked-test snapshot mode reportedly loses independently installed nested package dependencies.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,context-management,github-intake
created_at: "2026-09-30T06:48:35.183Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-02T21:29:20.281Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-02T21:29:19.023Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-02T21:29:19.023Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Real filesystem regression retains distinct root and nested dependency versions without flattening; Snapshot and ordinary linked runs preserve PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH isolation; Dependency write/isolation behavior is documented and tested; Current built and packed artifacts pass the reporter contract
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "The shared SDK snapshot resolves the physical workspace root, preserves every installed root/nested dependency path by original-tree junction, rebases included file and directory aliases into the copy, preserves dangling-file isolation, and refuses external or excluded source aliases before execution."
expected_result: Linked snapshots retain each original dependency resolution tree while writes to copied source and included source aliases remain disposable; dependency writes require an independent installation.
actual_result: Owner-linked test-local-murgw94f-a8ye79 passes seven real filesystem/CLI cases. Manual temporary Node and Bun workflows resolve distinct root/nested npm versions and preserve original source bytes through file/directory/dangling aliases. Shared canonical test-local-murgv9bh-hqiwl4 passes 9616 tests at exact all-source 100/100/100/100; packed npm/npx/bunx/SDK and 89-command dogfood pass. Native Windows remains required on the pushed head.
