comments[15]:
  - created_at: "2026-09-30T06:48:35.183Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus contained 2843 records with no unreadable directories or items. Exact GitHub ID plus behavior/root-cause searches were complete. Closed prior lineage pm-efkvdy and its full history were read; this new report requests a distinct unimplemented contract. Relationship reconstructed during current intake rather than asserted as historical knowledge. Queued and unclaimed; source investigation remains pending."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T16:39:25.373Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Actively implementing this dependency-resolution contract in the same substantial PR as pm-r61juc: preserving nested dependency identity and isolated tracker roots is required for genuine package/security acceptance. Original reporter and full current item/history read; pre-fix reproduction and real filesystem regression precede implementation. Unrelated roadmap items remain open and unclaimed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T16:44:09.145Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Pre-edit test audit: primary owner is the existing linked-test workspace integration suite at the public CLI boundary. The regression imports different locally installed root/nested package versions through real filesystem resolution and verifies sandbox environment and source-file preservation. Existing workspace-mode tests have no nested dependency directory, so root-only linking falsely passes them. No test-only SDK export or control is needed. The unchanged new test must fail before the source fix."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T17:04:51.086Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Verification: the new CLI filesystem regression failed before the fix because the nested dependency resolved to root version 1.0.0 instead of independently installed 2.0.0. It now passes with both real directory and directory-link paths; source bytes are preserved, copied-file writes stay disposable, and PM roots remain isolated. Dependencies remain shared by convention, documented explicitly. The extraction gives the snapshot policy an independently measured coverage surface rather than placing new logic inside an existing orchestration ignore region."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T17:31:34.651Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Manual acceptance in a temporary monorepo installed fast-json-patch 3.1.1 at the root and 3.1.0 independently under apps/site. Real Node node:test and Bun linked runs both passed with pm_context_mode=none and workspace_context_mode=snapshot; nested resolution remained 3.1.0 and copied-source writes did not affect the original. Focused regression suites pass, including exclusions, external nested links, broken links, source preservation and Windows junction workflow contracts. Local npm module lookup required NODE_PATH pointing to the actual installed global npm package; no source workaround was added."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T18:00:21.989Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Broad validation: 9602 tests passed in the four-worker full run, with one unchanged reproducibility test exceeding its 30-second test budget. Its complete four-case suite plus release automation passed unchanged in a two-worker rerun (28 tests). No timeout, coverage threshold or test assertion was relaxed. A final full coverage run will use two workers and sequential local test jobs. Packed acceptance is independently verified; only source-copy writes, not dependency-tree writes, are isolated by snapshot mode."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T18:32:21.111Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final test audit: the complete two-worker canonical coverage run passed 9603 tests across 763 files (2 existing Windows-only skips), with statements 66406/66406, branches 50827/50827, functions 13731/13731 and lines 63329/63329. No source, coverage denominator, threshold or ignore policy changed afterward. The final integration fixture now unconditionally proves absent PM_PATH in none context and performs a real copied-workspace write; all four linked trust/workspace cases pass. Real temporary npm root/nested 3.1.1/3.1.0 installations passed Node and Bun snapshots, packed npm/npx/bunx and SDK consumer smoke passed, compatibility passed. Dependency trees are shared by convention; copied regular-source writes are disposable, not an OS security sandbox."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T18:35:03.052Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final local delivery: both owner-linked commands passed through pm test --run --progress with trusted same-branch provenance and sandboxed tracker roots. Snapshot suite: 6 tests in 2 files; security/release/workflow suite: 44 tests in 4 files. Package-first dogfood now passes after sequential execution; the earlier timeout was competing build-lease contention, not a relaxed test. Complete static gates, including unchanged SDK startup budgets, graph composition, record integrity and bounded mutation (329 killed, 7 classified equivalent, 0 failures), pass."
    edited_at: "2026-10-02T18:35:36.652Z"
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T19:08:09.209Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "PR 1375 review regressions: relative source roots now produce absolute dependency junction targets. Dangling dependency links are ignored using stat with throwIfNoEntry false, avoiding the Windows access/stat disagreement seen in native CI. Both real-filesystem unit tests pass locally, and hosted Windows remains the independent platform acceptance gate. Full canonical source coverage is executed once under pm-r61juc and shared through the typed verification relationship rather than duplicating the complete suite."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T19:43:04.577Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Shared canonical coverage is auditable in pm-r61juc run test-local-murdbyvj-6ohpqa: the actual linked full-suite command passed with 9608 passing tests and two existing Windows-only skips. Statements 66411/66411, branches 50825/50825, functions 13734/13734 and lines 63334/63334 are exact covered/total counts, all 100 percent. The primary owner has four run-bound threshold measurements and a verifies relationship to this snapshot owner, avoiding duplicated complete-suite executions."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T20:21:55.779Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Round-two real filesystem TDD reproduced two source alias failures before implementation: an aliased workspace root retained original-source links and external/excluded aliases were accepted. Preserve dependency sharing deliberately, but resolve the source root and rebase ordinary within-workspace aliases into copied source; refuse targets outside included source. Genuine directory, file and dangling file controls cover source preservation."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T21:00:43.159Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Revised manual acceptance in a fresh temporary monorepo passes actual Node node:test and Bun linked snapshots with independently installed fast-json-patch 3.1.1 root and 3.1.0 nested. Both write through file and absolute directory source aliases and create through a dangling file alias inside the disposable copy; original identity bytes and absent source file remain unchanged. Temporary data is cleaned and tracker roots remain isolated."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T21:21:06.870Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Shared frozen-source proof: pm-r61juc canonical receipt test-local-murgv9bh-hqiwl4 passes 9616 tests, 762 suites and exact all-source 100/100/100/100. Its linked report receipt test-local-murgvxx1-115b0n records covered/total counts and the generated-report SHA-256 without duplicating the full suite. Real temporary CLI acceptance independently passes under both Node and Bun with root and nested fast-json-patch installations, included source file/directory aliases and dangling-file writes confined to the disposable snapshot. Source target bytes and absence of the dangling original remain intact; both temporary workspaces were cleaned."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T21:22:15.983Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Owner-linked receipt test-local-murgw94f-a8ye79 passes seven cases across the real filesystem snapshot policy and CLI integration. It covers original root/nested dependency identities, included source alias rebasing, dangling-file isolation, external/excluded refusal and independently installed nested versions. The source is unchanged since the complete canonical proof; native Windows junction and file-symlink acceptance remains required on the pushed head."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T21:29:11.472Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: Packed npm/npx/bunx and installed SDK consumers pass after the snapshot source-alias fixes. The 89-command isolated package-first dogfood journey passes and cleans its temporary tracker. Node/Bun manual alias acceptance and the owner-linked seven-case suite preserve source bytes and distinct dependency installations. Native Windows acceptance will be checked on the pushed revision.
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T18:32:24.044Z","harness:codex",Snapshot dependency preservation must retain each nested installation at its original relative path. Positive direct execution plus a real copied-workspace write distinguishes correct dependency resolution from a no-op isolation assertion. Directory junctions retain Windows support; dependency writes still require an independent install or stronger sandbox.
  "2026-10-02T20:36:49.004Z","harness:codex",A disposable workspace must also rebase ordinary source aliases and resolve an aliased workspace root. Blind dereferencing can import excluded tracker data or external files. Preserve included source link topology inside the copy and refuse outside or excluded targets; dependency links are a separate deliberately shared contract.
